# std-program's cases whose log holds `avra: while running `, one a line, by the first line the runner
# says after it. The gate fails on a trap this file does not list.
#
# packages/std-program/src/tests/disk_store_test.av:389
#   the case's own worker traps by design (`echo_or_trap`): a forked share dies and the asking process
#   answers what it held; the case itself runs to its answer
disk_store — answers outlive the process / a process that traps before finishing its share / the share it held is answered by the asking process, and every answer comes out right
#
# packages/std-program/src/tests/disk_store_test.av:424
#   the same by design: the worker traps at its first turn and the asking process answers its item
disk_store — answers outlive the process / a process that traps at its first turn / the item it held is answered by the asking process, and every answer comes out right
